Z||000000||ggarsk||08-21-99||02:50 AM||||Hi all! I'm a new Fiero owner and I must thank all of you for your info on clutch problems. When I bought the car the owner said the slave cylinder was bad. I ordered a repair kit for it,but I also got the replacement steel clutch petal. I installed that first.Without touching the slave cylinder my car shifts like a dream. I would recommend that you replace the pedal and maybe it will clear up your chronic clutch problems. the only thing that I have to add to v8archies excellent instructions is that you will need a pair of pedal shaft bushings. You can get them at auto part stores. They are in the Help line of replacement parts. The part number is 74016. If you have any questions just leave a reply and I'll try to answer them.
